---
// Public — reachable without a session (src/middleware.ts's
// PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_PATHS). Left statically prerendered like terms.astro/
// privacy.astro, its two companion documents: no per-request data, and
// a visitor deciding whether to register needs to be able to read it
// before creating an account.
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Research Use Policy"
  description="What Cloud Peptides is for, who it's for, and the research-only terms every account agrees to."
  lastUpdated="August 13, 2026"
>
  <h2>Who this site is for</h2>
  <p>
    Cloud Peptides is restricted to independent researchers and authorized representatives of
    legitimate research organizations accessing this site for lawful educational or non-clinical
    laboratory research purposes. Every account is reviewed against this standard at registration
    through the Researcher Certification, and every account holder agrees to it again whenever the
    certification is materially updated.
  </p>

  <h2>Educational and scientific research purpose only</h2>
  <p>
    The information available through this website — compound research profiles, evidence summaries,
    citations, regulatory records, and administration-route context — is provided solely for
    educational and scientific research purposes. It is not medical advice, prescribing information,
    treatment guidance, or a substitute for consultation with a qualified healthcare professional.
    See our <a href="/disclaimer">Research and Medical Disclaimer</a> for how our published claims are
    sourced and reviewed.
  </p>

  <h2>Shop materials are for non-clinical laboratory research only</h2>
  <p>
    All materials offered through the Cloud Peptides shop are intended exclusively for legitimate,
    non-clinical laboratory research. They are not intended for human or veterinary consumption,
    administration, therapeutic use, diagnostic use, food use, cosmetic use, or household use. By
    creating an account, a researcher agrees not to ingest, inject, inhale, apply, implant, or
    otherwise administer any Cloud Peptides research material to a human or animal, and not to use
    or represent these materials for the diagnosis, treatment, mitigation, cure, or prevention of
    any disease or medical condition.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibility as a researcher</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for confirming that you are legally permitted to access and handle the
    relevant research materials in your jurisdiction, and for complying with all applicable laws,
    regulations, institutional requirements, and safety procedures that apply to you or your
    organization. Laws governing research chemicals and peptides vary by location and change over
    time — see also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens if this policy is violated</h2>
  <p>
    Providing false information during registration, or using Cloud Peptides materials contrary to
    this policy or the Researcher Certification, may result in immediate account suspension or
    termination.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Existing account holders can reach us through the contact options available after sign-in. For a
    question that must reach us before creating an account, email
    <a href="mailto:info.order.thecloud@proton.me">info.order.thecloud@proton.me</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
